##Project 4 - AI-Powered Project Status Reporting Automation.md

1. Project Overview

This project focuses on building an AI-powered project status reporting workflow using n8n.
The workflow will collect project task updates, analyse progress against planned activities, identify overdue tasks and potential delays, and generate a structured project status report using AI.
The objective is to demonstrate how workflow automation and AI can reduce manual reporting efforts, improve project visibility, and support timely decision-making.

## 2. Problem Statement
Project Managers often spend considerable time collecting updates from team members, reviewing task progress, identifying delays, and preparing project status reports.
When project information is maintained across spreadsheets and other tools, consolidating updates manually can become repetitive and time-consuming. It can also make it difficult to identify overdue activities and emerging delivery risks promptly.
This project addresses these challenges by automating the collection and analysis of project task data and using AI to generate clear, structured status reports that support project monitoring and decision-making.

## 3. Project Objectives
The objectives of this project are to:

- Automate the collection of project task updates from a central data source.
- Monitor task progress against planned deadlines.
- Identify completed, ongoing, pending, and overdue tasks.
- Calculate overall project progress using task data.
- Use AI to generate structured project status reports.
- Highlight potential delays and issues requiring the Project Manager's attention.
- Reduce manual reporting efforts and improve project visibility.

## 4. Tools and Technologies
The project will use the following tools and technologies:

n8n: Workflow automation and orchestration.
Google Sheets: Centralised storage of project tasks, deadlines, owners, and progress updates.
Google Gemini: AI-powered analysis and generation of project status reports.
JavaScript: Basic data processing and calculations where required.
Gmail: Automated delivery of generated project status reports.

## 5. Workflow Design
The automation will follow this sequence:
- Workflow Trigger: Initiate the reporting process manually or at a scheduled interval.
- Retrieve Project Data: Fetch task records from Google Sheets.
- Process Task Information: Organise task details, calculate progress, and identify overdue activities.
- AI Analysis: Send the processed project information to Google Gemini for analysis and report generation.
- Format Status Report: Structure the AI-generated report into clear sections covering overall progress, completed tasks, ongoing activities, overdue tasks, and potential concerns.
- Email Notification: Send the generated report to the designated recipient through Gmail.
The workflow is designed to reduce manual reporting while keeping the Project Manager informed about project progress and activities requiring attention.

